                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Magic Hour successfully delivers a relaxing, high-fidelity simulation fix by blending immersive virtual reality physics with a structured, exploration-driven environment focused on VR photography. While the premise of a choice-driven camera training routine initially looks like a simple early access experiment, spending exactly 25 minutes inside the client is more than enough to see that the execution delivers a highly focused and mechanically accurate technical run.The central feature that reinforces the experience is its authentic virtual SLR engine. Instead of simplified arcade photo modes or predictable visual phases, the core gameplay channels entirely into a realistic exposure layout where adjusting actual aperture, shutter speed, and focal length values dictates the quality of your saved framework. It functions perfectly as a clean, stable prototype that values mechanical depth over artificial grind blocks. On the positive side, it successfully respects your active Steam showcase by completely omitting tedious or broken tracking achievements, while fully respecting your actual gaming time for a rewarding, scenic deployment. Do not skip this deployment",
